cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "PySVOrbit: A Python Package for Combined Spectroscopic and Visual Orbit Fitting for Binary Stars"
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the accompanying paper."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Al-Wardat
    given-names: Mashhoor A.
    affiliation: "Department of Applied Physics and Astronomy, University of Sharjah"
  - family-names: Talafha
    given-names: Mohammed H.
    affiliation: "Research Institute of Sciences and Engineering, University of Sharjah"
    email: mtalafha901@gmail.com
  - family-names: Alshamsi
    given-names: Shaikha N.
    affiliation: "Research Institute of Sciences and Engineering, University of Sharjah"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/mtalafha90/rvorbitwebpage"
url: "https://pysvorbit.onrender.com/"
abstract: >-
  PySVOrbit fits Keplerian orbits of binary stars to relative astrometry
  and radial-velocity measurements, jointly or separately, by weighted
  non-linear least squares, and derives the associated dynamical masses.
keywords:
  - astronomy
  - binary stars
  - orbit determination
  - astrometry
  - radial velocities
